        "width": "520",
        "height": "380",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "HT5 · Sacroiliac joint check (the joint between the base of the spine and the pelvis) — Laslett cluster\nSix pain-provocation tests: distraction, thigh thrust, compression, sacral thrust, and Gaenslen’s test on each side. Count those that reproduce the familiar pain.\nEVIDENCE: 3 or more of 6 positive: sensitivity 94%, specificity 78%. If ALL are negative, the sacroiliac joint can be ruled out (Laslett 2005; compared with diagnostic injections).\nRUN ONLY AFTER the back screen (H10).\nWHO: physio-level"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:5:868",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "5:868",
        "x": "7825",
        "y": "1271",
        "width": "280",
        "height": "153",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Below the dimples of the low back; after pregnancy or a fall onto the buttock"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:5:912",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "5:912",
        "x": "8360",
        "y": "1540",
        "width": "520",
        "height": "419",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "HD11 · WORKING DIAGNOSIS: Deep gluteal syndrome (includes “piriformis syndrome”)\nWHAT IT IS: irritation of the sciatic nerve deep in the buttock.\nCONFIRM: tender deep in the buttock; a seated stretch with the hip bent, crossed and turned inward reproduces buttock or sciatica-like pain — AND spine, sacroiliac joint and hamstring have been cleared. A diagnosis of exclusion; low certainty without imaging or nerve studies.\nNEXT STEP: cautious hip strengthening (outward rotators, abductors), sitting breaks and a softer seat (consensus).\nAVOID: forceful stretches that bring on nerve symptoms.\nWATCH: re-test at week 4; worsening nerve signs → doctor.\nSTAGE 3 ADD-ON: hamstring module."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:5:872",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "5:872",
        "x": "8480",
        "y": "1271",
        "width": "280",
        "height": "199",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Deep buttock pain with sitting, sometimes sciatica-like, and everything else is negative"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:5:856",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
