        "width": "520",
        "height": "426",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "HD8 · WORKING DIAGNOSIS: Meralgia paresthetica (squeezed skin nerve of the thigh)\nWHAT IT IS: the lateral femoral cutaneous nerve — a skin-sensation nerve — is pinched where it passes the front of the pelvic bone. Causes: tight belts, tool belts, waist-tied saris or dhotis, pregnancy, weight change, diabetes.\nCONFIRM: a patch of burning, tingling or numbness on the outer-front thigh, with NORMAL strength (light-touch map compared with the other side).\nNEXT STEP: loosen belts and waistbands; explain it is a nerve, not the joint. Not an exercise condition (consensus).\nREFER IF: any weakness, or it spreads → back problem (H10) or doctor."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:5:744",
